  ('ode', 1, 'ode to joy', 'Many composers have written an ode to joy, celebrating happiness through music.', '许多作曲家创作过颂歌，赞美音乐中的快乐。', 'culture'),
  ('ode', 2, 'ode on a grecian urn', 'In literature, the ode on a Grecian urn explores beauty and mortality intricately.', '在文学中，颂歌对古希腊瓦罐的解析深入探讨了美与死亡。', 'academic'),
  ('ode', 3, 'ode to the west wind', 'Reading the ode to the west wind inspires feelings of change and renewal.', '阅读对西风的颂歌激发了改变与重生的情感。', 'daily_life'),
  ('whimsy', 1, 'whimsy in art', 'Artists often incorporate whimsy in their works to engage viewers.', '艺术家们常在作品中融入奇思妙想，以吸引观众。', 'culture'),
  ('whimsy', 2, 'whimsy of nature', 'The whimsy of nature can be seen in the unique shapes of trees.', '自然的奇思妙想可以在树木独特的形状中看到。', 'environment'),
  ('whimsy', 3, 'whimsy of design', 'Home decor often embraces the whimsy of design to create a playful atmosphere.', '家居装饰常常采用设计的奇思妙想，以营造一种轻松的氛围。', 'daily_life'),
  ('largesse', 1, 'largesse from wealthy donors', 'Many cultural institutions rely on largesse from wealthy donors to thrive.', '许多文化机构依赖富有捐赠者的慷慨来繁荣。', 'culture'),
